# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/maps/moors_delve.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event moor_peat_cutters
# en: The Peat Banks
title [f03f1d] = 泥炭坡
# en: {~The peat-cutters are working the long bank below the first cairn, slicing turves as neat as bread and stacking them to dry. Every seventh turf they cut a little cross into before they set it down.|The peat-cutters are at the long bank, and one of them holds out a spare spade to you, eyebrows up.|The cutters are resting on the bank with bread and cold tea. They make room for you, and ask {at_home(): after your family|where you're lodging}.} {season == "winter": The bank steams in the cold.|Larks go up from the heather all round.}
text [2163a0] = {~割泥炭的人正在第一个石堆下面那道长坡上干活，把草皮切得像面包一样整齐，码起来晾干。每切到第七块，他们都要在上面刻一个小十字，才把它放下。|割泥炭的人在长坡上，其中一个朝你递过一把备用的铲子，扬了扬眉毛。|割泥炭的人坐在坡上歇着，吃面包、喝冷茶。他们给你挪出位置，问{at_home(): 你家里人好不好|你住在哪儿}。} {season == "winter": 泥炭坡在寒气里冒着热气。|云雀从四周的石楠丛里飞起。}
# en: Peat-cutters in shirtsleeves cutting dark wet turves from a long bank on open moorland, stacks of drying peat behind them, a student watching.
scene [2e8321] = 开阔的荒原上，几个只穿衬衫的割泥炭人正从一道长坡上切下湿黑的草皮，身后堆着晾晒的泥炭，一个学生在旁边看着。
# en: Cut turves with them
opt.left.label [e628ec] = 跟他们一起割
# en: {~You cut eleven turves, badly, and get peat to the elbows and a crick in your back. They praise every one. You notice none of yours is the seventh.|Your back aches by noon. A cutter shows you how to lean on the spade, and the work goes easier.|You cut until your hands blister. When you ask how long they've cut this bank, the cutters talk about the weather.}
opt.left.say.1 [40b1d9] = {~你割了十一块，割得很糟，泥炭一直沾到手肘，腰也扭了。他们每一块都夸。你注意到，你割的没有一块是第七块。|不到中午你的腰就酸了。一个割泥炭的人教你怎么靠在铲子上使劲，活儿就轻松些了。|你一直割到手上起了水泡。你问他们这道坡割了多少年，他们却聊起了天气。}
# en: Ask about the moor
opt.right.label [69d1d9] = 问问荒原的事
# en: {~"Past the third cairn it goes on," says the eldest. "Don't go on with it." The others laugh, and then don't.|They tell you the bog roads are older than the villages, and the cairns older than the roads. Nobody knows who built the hill.|"Keep the cairns on your left going out," a cutter says, "and on your right coming back. And come back."}
opt.right.say.1 [591c9c] = {~“过了第三个石堆，它就一直往前延，”最年长的那个说。“别跟着它往前走。”其他人笑了，然后又不笑了。|他们告诉你，那些泥沼路比村子还老，石堆比路还老。没人知道那座山是谁堆的。|“出去的时候让石堆在你左边，”一个割泥炭的人说，“回来的时候让它们在你右边。还有，要回来。”}

@event moor_bilberries
# en: Bilberries
title [8f76ec] = 越橘
# en: {The slope above the road is blue with bilberries, and nobody else is picking them.|The bilberry slope again, and still nobody picking. The shepherds say they're for the birds.|You know the best patch now, below a split rock where the berries are fat as thumbnails.}
text [6dfb74] = {路上方的山坡被越橘染成了一片蓝，却没有别人来摘。|又是那片越橘坡，还是没人摘。牧羊人说那是留给鸟吃的。|你现在知道最好的那一片了，就在一块裂开的石头下面，果子大得像拇指甲。}
# en: A student kneeling among low bilberry bushes on a sunny moorland slope, purple-stained fingers, a tin half full, the valley far below.
scene [09df6e] = 阳光下的荒原山坡上，一个学生跪在低矮的越橘丛中，手指染成紫色，铁罐装了一半，山谷远在下方。
# en: Fill a tin
opt.left.label [74e3d4] = 装满一罐
# en: {You fill the tin and your mouth. Your fingers are purple for two days. You buy a pie dish at the market for them, which seems only right.|An hour of picking in the sun, with the whole valley below you and the larks going up. You buy cream for them in the village.|You eat as many as you keep. The tin of cream from the inn costs more than the tin of berries is worth, and it doesn't matter.}
opt.left.say.1 [7a03df] = {你装满了罐子，也塞满了嘴。手指紫了两天。你在集市上为它们买了个馅饼盘，这才说得过去。|在太阳底下摘了一个钟头，整个山谷在你脚下，云雀不断飞起。你在村里买了奶油来配。|你吃的和留的一样多。从客栈买的那罐奶油比那罐越橘还贵，可这无所谓。}
# en: Just sit in the sun
opt.right.label [9b3a7b] = 就坐着晒晒太阳
# en: {You sit in the heather and do nothing for an hour, and get sunburnt on one side.|You watch the shadows of clouds cross the valley. The wind turns cold all at once, and you walk back stiff.|You lie back and doze. When you wake, there's a sheep standing over you, and your neck is stiff.}
opt.right.say.1 [17abed] = {你坐在石楠丛里什么也不干，坐了一个钟头，结果半边脸晒伤了。|你看着云影一片片掠过山谷。风一下子变冷了，你僵着身子走回去。|你往后一躺，打起盹来。醒来时，一只羊正站在你上方，你的脖子也僵了。}

@event moor_edge
# en: Past the Third Cairn
title [b2c540] = 过了第三个石堆
# en: {moor_deepest == 0: A shepherd on the road tells you to stay this side of the third cairn, then walks off before you can ask why. Past it, the heather goes on, and the fog is coming up in the hollows, unhurried.|{~The third cairn, and past it the moor going on longer than it should.|The third cairn. Past it the wind changes, as if at a line.|Fog in the hollows past the third cairn, and the heather waiting.}} {flag(moor_drove_road): You know where the shepherds' trod leaves the sheep track.|}
text [888d5f] = {moor_deepest == 0: 路上一个牧羊人叫你待在第三个石堆这一边，你还没来得及问为什么，他就走了。过了那里，石楠一直往前延，雾正从洼地里不慌不忙地升起来。|{~第三个石堆，过了它，荒原延伸得比该有的更远。|第三个石堆。过了它，风向就变了，像是到了一条界线。|第三个石堆过去的洼地里起了雾，石楠在等着。}} {flag(moor_drove_road): 你知道牧羊人小道从哪儿离开羊肠小路。|}
# en: A tall grey cairn on open moorland, a sheep track running past it into rising fog, a student standing beside the cairn looking on.
scene [f2baab] = 开阔的荒原上一个高高的灰色石堆，一条羊肠小路从它旁边伸进升起的雾里，一个学生站在石堆旁望着前方。
# en: Stay this side
opt.left.label [dbf937] = 待在这一边
# en: {~You touch the cairn and turn back. The moor is quite big enough from here.|Not today. You watch the fog fill the hollows from the road, which is the sensible place to watch it from.|You stay this side. A sheep watches you not go, and seems satisfied.}
opt.left.say.1 [4753f9] = {~你摸了摸石堆，转身回去。从这儿看，荒原已经够大了。|今天不了。你站在路上看雾填满洼地，路上本来就是看雾的明智之处。|你待在这一边。一只羊看着你没往前走，似乎很满意。}
# en: Go on past it
opt.right.label [b481d5] = 走过去
# en: A delve: press on card by card, turn back any time.
opt.right.hint [e6594e] = 一场探险：一张接一张往深处走，随时可以回头。
# en: {flag(moor_drove_road): You find the shepherds' trod where the shepherd showed you, and follow it straight out past the easy ground.|{at_home() and moor_deepest == 0: You go past the third cairn the way you did as a child on a dare, and this time you don't run back.|You go past the third cairn. Behind you, the road and the villages are suddenly very small.}}
opt.right.say.1 [8ab550] = {flag(moor_drove_road): 你在牧羊人指给你的地方找到了牧羊人小道，顺着它径直走过了好走的那一段。|{at_home() and moor_deepest == 0: 你像小时候被人激将那样走过了第三个石堆，这回你没有跑回来。|你走过了第三个石堆。在你身后，那条路和那两个村子一下子变得很小。}}

@event moor_way_home
# en: Off the Moor
title [25f8aa] = 下了荒原
# en: {moor_haul == 0: You come down off the moor with nothing but wet boots and the feeling of being counted.|{moor_haul <= 2: You come down off the moor with a light bag: a flint or two, a fleece-tuft of bog cotton, something old.|{moor_haul <= 4: You come down off the moor with a bag that clinks: flints, old bronze, a stone with a hole in it.|You come down off the moor bent under a heavy bag, and the fog lets you go reluctantly.}}} {moor_depth >= 5: Your boots are black with the hill's peat.|}
text [d673c3] = {moor_haul == 0: 你从荒原上下来，除了一双湿靴子，只有一种被人数过的感觉。|{moor_haul <= 2: 你从荒原上下来，包里轻轻的：一两块燧石，一缕羊毛似的棉草，还有一样老东西。|{moor_haul <= 4: 你从荒原上下来，包里叮当作响：燧石、旧青铜，还有一块带孔的石头。|你从荒原上下来，被沉甸甸的包压弯了腰，雾不情不愿地放你走了。}}} {moor_depth >= 5: 你的靴子被那座山的泥炭染得乌黑。|}
# en: A tired student coming down off the moor onto a village road at evening, a lumpy bag over one shoulder, fog behind them on the heights.
scene [3285ad] = 傍晚，一个疲惫的学生从荒原上走下来，踏上村道，一只鼓鼓囊囊的包搭在肩上，身后高处是雾。
# en: Sell it at the inn
opt.left.label [b3878b] = 拿到客栈去卖
# en: Crowns, by what you carry.
opt.left.hint [0ece3c] = 克朗，按你带回的东西算。
# en: {moor_haul == 0: The landlord looks at your empty bag and gives you a hot drink anyway, on the house, and asks how far out you went.|{~The landlord of the coaching inn buys the lot for more than it's worth and wants to know exactly where you found each piece.|The landlord weighs it in his hands, pays you well, and puts it all in a box under the counter. He asks whether you'll be going out again.|The landlord pays without haggling, which is worse than haggling, and writes something in his little book.}}
opt.left.say.1 [4b415c] = {moor_haul == 0: 老板看看你空空的包，照样给了你一杯热饮，说是店里请的，又问你走出去多远。|{~驿站客栈的老板把东西全买下了，出的价比它们值的还高，还想知道每一件你是在哪儿找到的。|老板把东西掂了掂，付了你一笔好价钱，全放进柜台底下的一只箱子里。他问你还会不会再出去。|老板一点没还价就付了钱，这比还价还糟，然后在他的小本子上记了点什么。}}
# en: Keep it for study
opt.right.label [2aa44b] = 留着研究
# en: Lore and alchemy, by what you carry.
opt.right.hint [e49b16] = 学识和炼金，按你带回的东西算。
# en: {moor_haul == 0: You keep nothing but wet boots and a better idea of the moor.|{~You lay it all out on the washstand and spend the evening working out what's old, what's very old, and what shouldn't be here at all.|You clean the flints with a toothbrush and label everything. One bronze piece has a sheaf worked into it, worn almost away.|You sort it all by lamplight. The holed stone, held up to your eye, shows the room exactly as it is, which is somehow a relief.}}
opt.right.say.1 [f517a1] = {moor_haul == 0: 你什么也没留下，只有一双湿靴子，和对荒原多了几分了解。|{~你把东西全摆在洗脸架上，花了一晚上弄清哪些是老的，哪些是很老的，哪些根本不该在那儿。|你用牙刷把燧石刷干净，每样都贴上标签。有一件青铜器上铸着一束麦子，几乎磨平了。|你借着灯光把东西一一分好。那块带孔的石头举到眼前，看到的房间和原来一模一样，这不知怎么让人松了口气。}}

@event moor_stumble
# en: Back on Your Feet
title [8218be] = 重新站起来
# en: {~You go down hard in the heather, and something rolls out of your bag into a hag of black water.|You come to your senses face down in wet heather, with a split lip and a lighter bag.|Your foot finds the one soft place on the hill. You get free, and the bog keeps a little of what you carried.} {moor_grace > 0: You've got one more fall in you, maybe.|That was your last easy fall.}
text [a55ad0] = {~你重重摔倒在石楠丛里，包里有样东西滚了出去，掉进一洼黑水里。|你回过神来时，脸朝下趴在湿漉漉的石楠里，嘴唇裂了，包也轻了。|你一脚踩中了山上唯一一处软地。你挣脱出来，泥沼留下了你带着的一点东西。} {moor_grace > 0: 你大概还经得起再摔一次。|那是你最后一次摔得不算重。}
# en: A student sitting in wet heather on a foggy moor, catching their breath, a spilled bag beside them.
scene [e366ad] = 雾蒙蒙的荒原上，一个学生坐在湿石楠里喘气，身边是一只撒了一地的包。
# en: That's enough for today
opt.left.label [3d2940] = 今天就到这儿
# en: {~You pick up what's left and limp back toward the road.|You've had enough of the moor, and the moor of you.|You turn back, keeping the cairns on your right.}
opt.left.say.1 [90d7fe] = {~你捡起剩下的东西，一瘸一拐地朝路上走回去。|你受够了荒原，荒原也受够了你。|你转身回去，让石堆待在你右边。}
# en: Get up and go on
opt.right.label [813dfe] = 爬起来，继续走
# en: Deeper: the next fall may not be kind.
opt.right.hint [cae0c4] = 更深处：下一次摔倒未必这么轻。
# en: {~You wring out your sleeves and go on, a little slower.|You get up. The fog closes round again as if nothing had happened.|You go on. Somewhere behind you, a sheep bell stops.}
opt.right.say.1 [ed7b0a] = {~你拧干袖子，继续往前走，慢了一点。|你爬了起来。雾又合拢了，好像什么也没发生过。|你继续走。身后某处，一只羊铃不响了。}

@event moor_lost
# en: Found at Dusk
title [b09f99] = 黄昏时被找到
# en: {at_home() and has(origin_hedge): The fog comes down and the day goes with it. At dusk a lantern comes bobbing through the fog, and it's your grandmother, with a shawl and a flask and a face like thunder.|The fog comes down and the day goes with it. At dusk a dog finds you first, and then a shepherd with a lantern, who looks at you the way he'd look at a ewe that got itself stuck.}
text [d6d95c] = {at_home() and has(origin_hedge): 雾落下来，这一天也跟着没了。黄昏时，一盏提灯摇摇晃晃地穿过雾来，是你外婆，拿着披肩和一壶热饮，脸色难看得像要打雷。|雾落下来，这一天也跟着没了。黄昏时，先是一条狗找到了你，然后是一个提着灯的牧羊人，他看你的眼神，就像看一只把自己卡住了的母羊。}
# en: A foggy moor at dusk, a shepherd with a lantern and a dog helping a muddy, shivering student to their feet.
scene [3918ea] = 黄昏时雾蒙蒙的荒原上，一个提着灯、带着狗的牧羊人正扶一个满身泥浆、瑟瑟发抖的学生站起来。
# en: Thank them and go quietly
opt.left.label [10e7a7] = 谢过对方，默默回去
# en: {at_home() and has(origin_hedge): She walks you home without a word and puts you to bed with something bitter. In the morning she says, "Past the third cairn," as if that were a whole sentence, and it is.|He walks you down to the road and won't take a penny. "Past the third cairn," he says, shaking his head. "They always go past the third cairn."}
opt.left.say.1 [1f299a] = {at_home() and has(origin_hedge): 她一声不吭地陪你回家，给你喝了点苦东西，打发你上床。第二天早上她说：“过了第三个石堆。”好像这就是一整句话，而它确实是。|他陪你走到路上，一个便士也不肯收。“过了第三个石堆，”他摇着头说。“他们总是要走过第三个石堆。”}
# en: Ask how they knew to look
opt.right.label [91390b] = 问对方怎么知道来找
# en: {at_home() and has(origin_hedge): "The lights were out on the drovers' road at noon," she says. "They only do that when somebody's lost." She says it as flatly as the weather.|"The sheep told me," he says. "They all stood looking the one way." He means it.}
opt.right.say.1 [354dc8] = {at_home() and has(origin_hedge): “中午赶畜道上就亮起了灯，”她说。“只有在有人走丢的时候才会那样。”她说得平淡，就像在说天气。|“羊告诉我的，”他说。“它们全都朝着一个方向站着。”他是认真的。}

@thread moor_delve
# en: The moors
name [bbe8f6] = 荒原
# en: Past the third cairn, the moor goes on longer than it should.
premise [9cd7c3] = 过了第三个石堆，荒原就延伸得比该有的更远。
# en: You pulled a shepherd's ewe out of a gully. He showed you the shepherds' trod out past the cairns.
journal.1 [6f9ae0] = 你把牧羊人的一只母羊从沟里拉了上来。他带你走了那条穿过石堆的牧羊人小道。
# en: Out on the bog road you found a traveller's satchel sunk in the peat, and a room key from the coaching inn.
journal.2 [5d0ddf] = 在泥沼路上，你发现一只陷在泥炭里的旅行挎包，里面有驿站客栈的一把房间钥匙。
# en: Seven cairns ring the hollow hill. One of them is new.
journal.3 [5ce928] = 七个石堆围着那座空心山。其中一个是新的。
# en: The black ram of the hollow hill gave way to you.
journal.4 [727151] = 空心山上的黑公羊给你让了路。
# en: There's a door in the side of the hollow hill, and it's shut.
journal.5 [10f989] = 空心山的一侧有一扇门，关着。

@event moor1_cairn
# en: A Stone for the Cairn
title [9379ce] = 给石堆添一块石头
# en: {~Out here the cairns are close together, each just in sight of the last, and every walker who passes adds a stone. The peat-cutters say it's for luck. The shepherds say it's so the cairn knows you went by.|The next cairn, and the next. Each one taller than the last, as if more people went this far than came back from further.}
text [3093c6] = {~这一带的石堆挨得很近，每一个都刚好看得见上一个，每个路过的人都要添一块石头。割泥炭的人说这是求个好运。牧羊人说这是让石堆知道你走过。|下一个石堆，再下一个。一个比一个高，好像走到这么远的人，比从更远处回来的人多。}
# en: A student setting a fist-sized stone on top of a tall moorland cairn, the next cairn faint in the fog beyond.
scene [1518e1] = 一个学生把一块拳头大的石头放到荒原上一个高高的石堆顶上，下一个石堆在前方雾里若隐若现。
# en: Turn back here
opt.left.label [3fbec1] = 就在这儿回头
# en: {~You leave the cairn as it is and turn back toward the road.|You decide the cairn is a sign, and the sign says home.}
opt.left.say.1 [dd1164] = {~你没动石堆，转身朝路上走回去。|你认定这石堆是个记号，而记号说的是：回家。}
# en: Carry up a stone and add it
opt.right.label [b97b3a] = 搬一块石头上来添上
# en: {~You carry a good stone up from the beck, arms aching, and set it on top. Walking on, you feel noted, which is better than unnoticed out here.|You add your stone, knuckles scraped from prising it loose. The cairn is warm under your hand, though the day is cold.}
opt.right.say.1 [95822c] = {~你从小溪边搬上来一块好石头，胳膊都酸了，把它放在顶上。往前走时，你觉得自己被记下了，在这儿，这比没人注意要好。|你添上你的石头，撬它的时候指节都擦破了。天很冷，石堆在你手下却是暖的。}

@event moor1_adders
# en: Adders in the Heather
title [999d25] = 石楠丛里的蝰蛇
# en: The sheep track crosses a flat warm stone, and the stone is covered in adders, a whole knot of them basking, zigzag-backed and in no hurry. One lifts its head and tastes the air in your direction.
text [03251a] = 羊肠小路穿过一块晒得暖暖的平石，石头上爬满了蝰蛇，一整团在晒太阳，背上是锯齿纹，一点也不着急。其中一条抬起头，朝你这边吐着信子。
# en: A knot of dark zigzag-backed adders basking together on a warm flat stone across a narrow sheep track in the heather.
scene [2a82b9] = 石楠丛中一条窄窄的羊肠小路上，一团背上带锯齿纹的深色蝰蛇正盘在一块暖和的平石上晒太阳。
# en: Back off and go home
opt.left.label [7ca8ab] = 退开，回家去
# en: {~You back away slowly, and give the stone a very wide berth all the way home.|You leave the stone to the adders. They have the sun; you have your ankles.}
opt.left.say.1 [8eaa35] = {~你慢慢往后退，回家的一路上都离那块石头远远的。|你把石头留给蝰蛇。它们有太阳；你有脚踝。}
# en: Drive them off the track
opt.right.label [26490a] = 把它们赶下小路
# en: They come at you all at once: keep your guard up.
opt.right.hint [12394a] = 它们一拥而上：护住自己。
# en: {~The knot comes apart and pours away into the heather. Under the stone where they lay there's a shed skin, perfect, and an old bronze pin.|You see them off the stone. A shed adder skin lies across it like a dropped glove; you take it.}
opt.right.say.1 [b76dca] = {~那一团散开了，流水般钻进石楠里不见了。它们躺过的石头底下有一张完整的蜕皮，还有一枚旧青铜别针。|你把它们赶下了石头。一张蝰蛇蜕皮横在石头上，像一只掉下的手套；你把它收了起来。}
# en: {~They're faster than you are, and there are more of them. You leave the track with a swollen hand and your pride in shreds.|You never land a thing. You end up flat in the heather, heart going, hand burning.}
opt.right.say.2 [9cecc9] = {~它们比你快，而且比你多。你离开小路时手肿了，面子也碎了一地。|你一下也没打中。最后你平躺在石楠里，心怦怦直跳，手火辣辣地疼。}
# en: Chill the stone
opt.up.label [4f9b03] = 让石头变冷
# en: {~You lay a skin of frost across the stone. The adders go slow and sleepy and slide off into the heather, offended.|A breath of cold and the knot unwinds, sluggish, into the roots. You step over the frosted stone.}
opt.up.say.1 [77ee38] = {~你在石头上铺了一层霜。蝰蛇变得又慢又困，滑进石楠里去了，很不高兴。|一口寒气，那一团就松开了，懒洋洋地钻进根须里。你跨过那块结了霜的石头。}

@event moor1_lost_ewe
# en: A Ewe in the Gully
title [c50802] = 沟里的母羊
# en: Bleating from a gully. A ewe has got herself onto a ledge halfway down and can't get up or down. There's a red mark daubed on her fleece, a seven, very neat. Somewhere a dog is barking, too far off to help.
text [4584da] = 沟里传来咩咩的叫声。一只母羊跑到了半坡的一块石台上，上不去也下不来。它的羊毛上抹着一个红记号，是个七，写得很工整。远处有条狗在叫，离得太远，帮不上忙。
# en: A ewe with a red mark daubed on her fleece stuck on a ledge in a steep, wet moorland gully, a student leaning over the edge above her.
scene [32147e] = 一只羊毛上抹着红记号的母羊困在一道陡峭潮湿的荒原沟壑半腰的石台上，一个学生在上面探身往下看。
# en: Fetch the shepherd instead
opt.left.label [4aa77d] = 去叫牧羊人来
# en: {~You go back down to the road and tell the first shepherd you meet. He thanks you, and goes up with his dog, not hurrying.|You turn back. The bleating follows you a long way.}
opt.left.say.1 [0716d6] = {~你回到路上，告诉遇见的第一个牧羊人。他谢了你，带着狗上去了，一点也不急。|你转身回去。那咩咩声一路跟着你，跟了很远。}
# en: Climb down for her
opt.right.label [00da7a] = 爬下去救它
# en: {~You get her up, both of you scraped and furious. Her shepherd arrives with the dog just as you top out, and in thanks shows you the shepherds' trod, which goes out past the cairns as straight as a ruler.|You haul her up by the fleece. The shepherd, when he comes, looks at the seven on her side and then at you, and tells you where the shepherds' trod runs.}
opt.right.say.1 [bab1f3] = {~你把它弄了上来，你们俩都擦破了皮，都气呼呼的。你刚爬到顶，它的牧羊人就带着狗赶到了，为了谢你，他带你走了那条牧羊人小道，它穿过石堆，直得像把尺子。|你揪着羊毛把它拽了上来。牧羊人来了，看看它身上的七，又看看你，然后告诉你牧羊人小道从哪儿走。}
# en: {~The gully side comes away under your boot. You and a good deal of the moor go down it together.|You slip, slide, and end up on the ledge beside her. She looks at you with deep contempt.}
opt.right.say.2 [7f70cd] = {~沟壁在你靴子底下塌了。你和一大块荒原一起滑了下去。|你一滑，一溜，最后落在它旁边的石台上。它用深深的鄙夷看着你。}

@event moor1_peat_hag
# en: The Peat Hag
title [c807f6] = 泥炭崖
# en: {~A peat hag, a bank of black peat cut by the weather, stands across your way. In its face, where the rain has washed it, there are flints, and something that glints green.|The weather has opened the peat bank further since anyone last came. Old things stick out of it like raisins from a cake.}
text [2dbe7c] = {~一道泥炭崖横在你的路上，那是被风雨切开的一道黑泥炭坡。雨水冲刷过的崖面上露出燧石，还有一样东西闪着绿光。|自上次有人来过之后，风雨又把这道泥炭坡冲开了一些。老东西从里面戳出来，像蛋糕里的葡萄干。}
# en: A deep cut bank of black peat on a moor, a student digging into its face with a trowel, flints and a bronze glint in the wet peat.
scene [cd1f25] = 荒原上一道被切开的深深的黑泥炭坡，一个学生正用小铲挖它的坡面，湿泥炭里露出燧石和一点青铜的闪光。
# en: Leave it and turn back
opt.left.label [d1faaa] = 别管它，回头
# en: {~You leave the peat to keep what it's kept, and head back.|You turn back with clean hands, which is more than the peat-cutters ever manage.}
opt.left.say.1 [44d80f] = {~你让泥炭留着它留下的东西，往回走了。|你两手干干净净地回去了，这比割泥炭的人从来都强。}
# en: Dig into the face
opt.right.label [616785] = 往坡面里挖
# en: {~You dig out three flints and a bronze button gone green, and cut your thumb on the last flint. You're black to the elbow and very pleased.|You work a flint scraper out of the peat, as sharp as the day it was made, as your palm finds out. The peat closes over the hole as if it minded.}
opt.right.say.1 [9b2346] = {~你挖出三块燧石和一颗发绿的青铜纽扣，最后一块燧石还割破了你的拇指。你从手到肘都是黑的，却高兴得很。|你从泥炭里撬出一把燧石刮刀，锋利得跟刚做出来那天一样，你的手掌可以作证。泥炭合拢在那个洞上，好像它很介意。}

@event moor1_larks
# en: Open Moor
title [cb517e] = 开阔的荒原
# en: {~Wide moor under a huge sky, and the cairns marching on ahead.|Open moor, cotton grass nodding, and the fog keeping to the hollows.|A beck to cross on stepping stones, peat-brown and loud.} {season == "winter": Frost on the heather; a raven goes over, croaking.|Larks go up singing from the heather on every side.} For a while the moor is only a moor.
text [d5b707] = {~辽阔的天空下是广阔的荒原，石堆一个接一个往前排去。|开阔的荒原，棉草点着头，雾待在洼地里。|一条泥炭色的、哗哗作响的小溪，得踩着垫脚石过去。} {season == "winter": 石楠上结着霜；一只渡鸦呱呱叫着飞过。|云雀从四周的石楠丛里唱着飞起。} 有那么一阵，荒原只是荒原。
# en: A student walking a sheep track across wide open moorland under a huge sky, a line of cairns marching on ahead.
scene [807a6f] = 辽阔的天空下，一个学生沿着羊肠小路穿过开阔的荒原，前方一排石堆一个接一个延伸出去。
# en: Turn back while it's easy
opt.left.label [d572f3] = 趁好走赶紧回头
# en: {~You turn round while the going is good, and are on the road before the light changes.|You turn back while the fog still keeps to its hollows.|You turn back at the beck, with dry feet and a clear head.}
opt.left.say.1 [f25aac] = {~你趁着好走转身回去，天色还没变就回到了路上。|你趁雾还待在洼地里，转身回去了。|你在小溪边回头，脚是干的，脑子是清醒的。}
# en: Go on
opt.right.label [8d20dc] = 继续走
# en: {~You walk on, and the moor widens round you.|You go on, out past where the cairns are close together.|You go on. Somewhere past the beck, the moor goes quiet.}
opt.right.say.1 [80c5f7] = {~你继续往前走，荒原在你四周越展越宽。|你继续走，走过石堆挨得很近的那一段。|你继续走。过了小溪的某处，荒原安静了下来。}

@event moor2_black_dog
# en: The Black Dog
title [412609] = 黑狗
# en: A black dog is standing on the bog road ahead, as big as a calf, shaggy and wet, with eyes like two lamps behind glass. It isn't anybody's. When you stop, it stops; when you take a step, it takes one too, towards you.
text [0c49ac] = 泥沼路前面站着一条黑狗，有小牛那么大，毛又长又湿，眼睛像玻璃后面的两盏灯。它不是谁家的。你停，它也停；你迈一步，它也迈一步，朝你迈过来。
# en: A huge shaggy black dog with pale eyes standing on a sunken causeway across a foggy bog, blocking the way of a student with a lantern.
scene [fb96fa] = 一条长着苍白眼睛的巨大长毛黑狗站在雾蒙蒙的泥沼中一条下陷的堤道上，挡住了一个提灯学生的去路。
# en: Back away along the road
opt.left.label [f95cf0] = 沿路往后退
# en: {~You back away the whole length of the bog road. It watches you go, and doesn't follow, which is somehow worse.|You turn back. When you look round, the road behind you is empty, and the fog is full of dog-shaped shadows.}
opt.left.say.1 [eefec6] = {~你沿着整条泥沼路一路往后退。它看着你走，却没跟上来，这不知怎么更糟。|你转身回去。回头看时，身后的路空空的，雾里却满是狗形的影子。}
# en: Stand and face it
opt.right.label [ed6798] = 站住，面对它
# en: It vanishes into the fog and comes again: strike when it shows.
opt.right.hint [86ad0f] = 它会消失在雾里又再出现：等它露面时出手。
# en: {~It backs into the fog and is gone, leaving pawprints that fill with water and then aren't there. The peat-cutters won't believe you, and then they will.|You hold your ground until it gives way. It doesn't run; it simply isn't there, and the road goes on.}
opt.right.say.1 [685627] = {~它退进雾里不见了，留下的爪印积满了水，然后就没了。割泥炭的人不会信你的，后来又会信的。|你一直坚持到它让开。它没有逃；它只是不在那儿了，路继续往前延。}
# en: {~It comes out of the fog from the side you weren't watching. You go down in the bog, and when you get up it's gone.|It knocks you flat and stands over you, breathing cold. Then it walks away, as if it had made its point.}
opt.right.say.2 [dc1a18] = {~它从你没防着的那一边从雾里扑出来。你栽进泥沼，等你爬起来，它已经不见了。|它把你撞翻在地，站在你上方，呼出冷气。然后它走开了，像是已经把话说完了。}
# en: Light the road
opt.up.label [26771a] = 照亮这条路
# en: {~You raise a clean white light. The dog looks at it a long moment, then turns and pads away into the fog, unhurried.|In the starlight the dog is only a shadow, and then not even that. You walk on through where it stood. It's very cold there.}
opt.up.say.1 [35d7d2] = {~你举起一团干净的白光。那条狗盯着光看了很久，然后转身，不慌不忙地走进了雾里。|在星光里，那条狗只是一道影子，接着连影子也不是了。你走过它站过的地方。那里冷得很。}

@event moor2_bog_road
# en: The Bog Road
title [45fece] = 泥沼路
# en: The old road across the bog is made of oak planks laid end to end, older than anyone can say. Most are sound. Some are not. The water either side is black, and very still, and very patient.
text [3f6ba7] = 横穿泥沼的那条老路是用橡木板一块接一块铺成的，老得没人说得清有多老。大多数木板还结实。有些不是。两边的水黑沉沉的，很静，也很有耐心。
# en: An ancient timber trackway half-sunk in a black moorland bog, its planks slick and broken, a student testing one with a foot.
scene [572f67] = 一条古老的木板道半陷在漆黑的荒原泥沼里，木板又滑又破，一个学生正用脚试探其中一块。
# en: Turn back
opt.left.label [2f9f2d] = 回头
# en: {~You don't trust the planks, and they don't seem to trust you. You go home.|You decide the bog can keep its road.}
opt.left.say.1 [8edd60] = {~你信不过这些木板，木板好像也信不过你。你回家了。|你决定让泥沼留着它的路。}
# en: Cross on the planks
opt.right.label [f2d8c8] = 踩着木板过去
# en: {~Plank by plank, testing each one, you cross. Halfway over, one sinks under you and comes up again behind you, as if it had changed its mind.|You run the last stretch and make it, wet to the shin and grinning.}
opt.right.say.1 [af36cb] = {~一块接一块，每块都先试一试，你过去了。走到一半，有一块在你脚下沉了下去，又在你身后浮了上来，像是改变了主意。|最后一段你是跑过去的，你成功了，裤腿湿到小腿，咧着嘴笑。}
# en: {~A plank turns under your foot. You go into the bog to the waist, and it holds on to you with great affection.|You slip off the road into the black water. Getting out takes everything you've got, and one boot.}
opt.right.say.2 [9500d5] = {~一块木板在你脚下翻了。你掉进泥沼，水没到腰，它十分亲热地抓着你不放。|你从路上滑进了黑水里。爬出来用尽了你所有的力气，还丢了一只靴子。}
# en: Freeze the bog
opt.up.label [d71565] = 冻住泥沼
# en: {~You breathe frost across the water either side, and walk over a road of ice. Behind you it creaks back to bog.|The bog freezes white under your spell. Something under the ice moves away from you, slowly.}
opt.up.say.1 [c63e44] = {~你朝两边的水呼出一层霜，踩着一条冰路走了过去。在你身后，它又嘎吱嘎吱地变回了泥沼。|泥沼在你的咒语下冻得发白。冰下有什么东西慢慢地游开了，离你远远的。}

@event moor2_fog
# en: Fog from Nowhere
title [cd4e57] = 凭空起雾
# en: The fog comes up out of the ground all at once, and in a minute you can't see your own boots. Only the tops of the cairns show above it, grey heads in a white sea, in a line that leads on, or back, depending which way you count them.
text [44638d] = 雾一下子从地里冒了出来，一分钟之内你就看不见自己的靴子了。只有石堆的顶露在雾上，像白色海面上一颗颗灰色的脑袋，排成一行，往前或往回，就看你怎么数。
# en: Thick white fog covering a moor, only the dark tops of cairns showing above it in a line, a student standing in the fog up to the chest.
scene [5e0325] = 浓浓的白雾盖住了荒原，只有一排深色的石堆顶露在雾上，一个学生站在齐胸深的雾里。
# en: Count them back to the road
opt.left.label [056e39] = 数着石堆回到路上
# en: {~You count the cairns back one by one and come out on the road exactly where you went in.|You keep the cairns on your right and walk out of the fog into an ordinary afternoon.}
opt.left.say.1 [cf9146] = {~你一个一个数着石堆往回走，正好从你走进去的地方出来，回到了路上。|你让石堆待在你右边，走出了雾，回到一个平平常常的下午。}
# en: Count them on, deeper
opt.right.label [4cd45a] = 数着石堆往深处走
# en: {~You keep the count, cairn to cairn, and come out of the fog further on than you meant to, on a hillside you've never seen from the road.|You count them on, carefully. There's one more cairn than there should be, and you don't follow that one.}
opt.right.say.1 [bfa870] = {~你一个石堆接一个石堆地数下去，走出雾时，你比打算的走得更远，站在一片你从路上从没见过的山坡上。|你小心地往前数。石堆比该有的多出了一个，你没有跟着那一个走。}
# en: {~You lose the count at the ninth cairn, step towards a grey head in the fog, and walk straight off the edge of a peat hag.|You count wrong, or the cairns do. The cairn you were making for isn't there when you reach it, and neither is the ground.}
opt.right.say.2 [deac6c] = {~数到第九个石堆你就数乱了，你朝雾里一颗灰色的脑袋迈步，结果径直走下了一道泥炭崖的边。|你数错了，要不就是石堆数错了。你朝着走去的那个石堆，等你走到时并不在那儿，脚下的地也不在。}
# en: Gather a light about you
opt.up.label [bc80fb] = 聚起一团光
# en: {~You gather a guiding light around you, breath by breath. In its glow the fog keeps a polite distance, and the cairns come out of it one by one.|Your light gathers round you until the white thins to a ring you can walk in, and the next cairn is standing at its edge.}
opt.up.say.1 [e5ba7a] = {~你一口气一口气地在身周聚起一团引路的光。在它的光晕里，雾礼貌地保持着距离，石堆一个一个从雾里显出来。|你的光在身周聚拢，直到白雾薄成一圈你可以在里面走的环，下一个石堆就立在环的边上。}

@event moor2_satchel
# en: A Satchel in the Peat
title [af425c] = 泥炭里的挎包
# en: {flag(moor_inn_key): The satchel is still there in the peat beside the bog road, a little deeper than you left it. Someone has buckled it shut again.|Half sunk in the peat beside the bog road there's a satchel, good leather, the kind people buy for a journey. It's been here a long while. The buckle's green. Inside, wrapped in oilcloth, there's a brass room key on a wooden tag, and the tag is burned with the coaching inn's sign.}
text [2871ae] = {flag(moor_inn_key): 那只挎包还在泥沼路边的泥炭里，比你离开时陷得更深了一点。有人又把它扣上了。|泥沼路边的泥炭里半埋着一只挎包，上好的皮子，是人们出远门时买的那种。它在这儿很久了。扣环都绿了。里面用油布包着一把黄铜房间钥匙，系着一块木牌，木牌上烙着驿站客栈的招牌。}
# en: A good leather travelling satchel half sunk in black peat beside a moorland track, a student crouching over it holding up a brass room key on a wooden tag.
scene [f1fe93] = 荒原小路边，一只上好的皮质旅行挎包半陷在黑泥炭里，一个学生蹲在旁边，举着一把系着木牌的黄铜房间钥匙。
# en: Leave it and turn back
opt.left.label [d1faaa] = 别管它，回头
# en: {~You put it back as you found it and walk home faster than you meant to.|You leave the satchel to the peat. All the way back you can feel where it is, behind you.}
opt.left.say.1 [546b0c] = {~你把它照原样放回去，往家走得比打算的还快。|你把挎包留给泥炭。回去的一路上，你都能感觉到它在身后的什么地方。}
# en: Look inside and go on
opt.right.label [2b7668] = 看看里面，继续走
# en: {flag(moor_inn_key): You unbuckle it again. Empty now, except for peat water and a coaching-inn bill folded small, paid in full, for one night.|{~You pocket the key. It's heavier than a key should be. Room seven, the tag says, when you rub the peat off.|You take the key and leave the rest. Further on, you realise you've been holding it in your fist the whole way.}}
opt.right.say.1 [2e83e3] = {flag(moor_inn_key): 你又解开了它。现在是空的，只有泥炭水，和一张折得很小的驿站客栈账单，已付清，住一晚。|{~你把钥匙揣进兜里。它比一把钥匙该有的要沉。你擦掉泥炭，木牌上写着：七号房。|你拿了钥匙，其余的留下。走了一段，你才发现自己一路都把它攥在拳头里。}}

@event moor2_waymarks
# en: The Waymarks
title [5b4c3f] = 路标石
# en: {~Little standing stones mark the bog road here, knee-high and worn, one every hundred paces.|The bog road runs on between its waymarks, firm underfoot for once.|A waymark leans across the road, and someone has propped it straight with a turf.} Each stone has notches cut down its edge, in sevens. {season == "winter": Rime on the notches makes them easy to count.|Bog cotton blows across the road like the last of a snow.}
text [ba03cf] = {~这里的泥沼路边立着一块块小石碑，齐膝高，磨得很旧，每隔一百步一块。|泥沼路在路标石之间往前延，脚下难得结实了一回。|一块路标石斜倒在路上，有人用一块草皮把它撑正了。} 每块石头的边上都刻着一道道缺口，七个一组。{season == "winter": 缺口上结着霜，很容易数。|棉草被风吹过路面，像是最后一场雪。}
# en: A line of small worn standing stones marching along a sunken moorland road into the fog, each one notched along its edge, a student walking beside them.
scene [df3bd1] = 一排磨旧的小立石沿着一条下陷的荒原道路伸进雾里，每块石头边上都刻着缺口，一个学生走在它们旁边。
# en: Turn back along the road
opt.left.label [50e7cb] = 沿路回头
# en: {~You turn back, counting the stones off as you pass them, and they come out the same both ways.|You go back the way the waymarks came, which is the way they mean you to.|You leave the road to its stones and head home.}
opt.left.say.1 [942bd0] = {~你转身回去，路过一块就数一块，来回数出来的都一样。|你沿着路标石来的方向回去，那正是它们要你走的方向。|你把路留给它的石头，往家走了。}
# en: Walk on beside them
opt.right.label [0509a9] = 在它们旁边继续走
# en: {~You walk on. The notches get fewer the further you go, as if fewer people came this way.|You go on, stone to stone. The last notch on the last one is fresh.|You walk on. The fog parts ahead of the stones and closes behind them.}
opt.right.say.1 [e9575b] = {~你继续往前走。越往前，缺口越少，好像走到这儿的人越来越少。|你一块石头接一块石头地往前走。最后一块石头上的最后一道缺口是新刻的。|你继续走。雾在石头前面分开，又在它们后面合上。}

@event moor3_barrow_ram
# en: The Black Ram
title [d78563] = 黑公羊
# en: {flag(moor_ram_beaten): The black ram is on the hill again. It lowers its head when it sees you, but slowly, as if remembering.|On the slope of the hollow hill there's a ram, black as peat, with horns curled round twice, standing square across the only way up, as if it had been set there like a gate. It isn't grazing. It lowers its head.}
text [3a04c5] = {flag(moor_ram_beaten): 黑公羊又在山上了。它看见你，低下了头，却低得很慢，像是想起了什么。|空心山的山坡上有一只公羊，黑得像泥炭，角盘了两圈，方方正正地挡在唯一一条上山的路上，像是被人立在那儿当门的。它不吃草。它低下了头。}
# en: An enormous black ram with great curling horns standing on the green slope of a round hill in the fog, head lowered at a student below.
scene [c22cc5] = 雾中一座圆山的绿坡上，站着一只长着巨大盘角的黑色巨公羊，正低着头对着坡下的一个学生。
# en: Back down the hill
opt.left.label [c1fe68] = 退下山去
# en: {~You back down the slope. The ram watches you to the bottom, then goes back to standing.|You leave the hill to its ram. It doesn't follow; it doesn't need to.}
opt.left.say.1 [1aafd4] = {~你退下山坡。公羊一直看着你走到坡底，然后又接着站着。|你把这座山留给它的公羊。它没跟来；它也不需要跟来。}
# en: Face it
opt.right.label [20a309] = 面对它
# en: It scrapes before it charges: the blow comes next exchange.
opt.right.hint [9014fe] = 它冲之前会刨地：撞击在下一回合到来。
# en: {~It lowers its great head, snorts, and walks back up the hill as if the hill had sent for it. Where it stood there's a twist of black fleece caught on a thorn, soft as smoke.|It gives way at last, with dignity. You take the tuft of fleece it leaves on the thorn, and go up the slope it was guarding.}
opt.right.say.1 [9b9929] = {~它低下硕大的头，喷了个响鼻，走回了山上，好像是山把它叫回去的。它站过的地方，一丛荆棘上挂着一缕黑羊毛，软得像烟。|它终于让开了，让得很体面。你取下它留在荆棘上的那缕羊毛，走上了它守着的山坡。}
# en: {~You see the charge coming and still can't get out of its way. You come to at the bottom of the hill.|It butts you clean off the slope. You land in the heather a long way down, and the ram doesn't bother to look.}
opt.right.say.2 [0c050e] = {~你看着它冲过来，却还是躲不开。你醒来时已经在山脚下了。|它一头把你顶下了山坡。你落在远远下面的石楠丛里，公羊连看都懒得看一眼。}
# en: Ask it what it guards
opt.up.label [f0e476] = 问它在守着什么
# en: {~You ask it the right way. It doesn't speak, but the answer comes anyway, plain as a thought of your own: a door, and the ones who come to it. Then it steps aside.|You put the question to it, and the answer arrives in your head in a voice like wind over heather: the way in, and the way out, which are not the same. The ram lets you pass.}
opt.up.say.1 [e9406b] = {~你用对的方式问了它。它没有开口，答案却照样来了，清楚得像你自己的念头：一扇门，还有来到门前的人。然后它让到了一旁。|你把问题向它提出，答案在你脑子里响起，声音像风吹过石楠：进去的路，和出来的路，那不是同一条。公羊让你过去了。}

@event moor3_seven_cairns
# en: Seven Cairns
title [d3ae76] = 七个石堆
# en: {flag(moor_new_cairn): The seven cairns round the hollow hill again. The pale one has settled since you last saw it, and moss is starting on its north side.|Seven cairns stand round the foot of the hollow hill, evenly spaced, like the numbers on a clock with most of the numbers missing. Six are grey with lichen. The seventh is pale, the stones still sharp, the moss not started. Someone built it this year.}
text [561c22] = {flag(moor_new_cairn): 又是空心山周围的七个石堆。那个浅色的，自你上次见过以后已经沉实了些，北面开始长苔藓了。|七个石堆围在空心山脚下，间距均匀，像一面大半数字都缺了的钟。六个长满了灰色的地衣。第七个是浅色的，石头还很锋利，苔藓还没长起来。有人今年才堆起它。}
# en: Seven tall cairns standing in a ring around the foot of a round green hill on a moor, one of them pale and newly built, a student looking at it.
scene [86e77a] = 荒原上一座圆圆的绿山脚下，七个高高的石堆围成一圈，其中一个颜色很浅，是新堆的，一个学生正看着它。
# en: Turn back
opt.left.label [2f9f2d] = 回头
# en: {~You leave the ring of cairns and go home the long way round.|You don't like the new cairn, and you don't stay to find out why.}
opt.left.say.1 [ce0eee] = {~你离开那圈石堆，绕远路回了家。|你不喜欢那个新石堆，也没留下来弄清为什么。}
# en: Look closely at the pale cairn
opt.right.label [27dbf0] = 凑近看看那个浅色的石堆
# en: {flag(moor_new_cairn): You look again. Someone has tied a sprig of something green to its top stone with red thread, since you were last here.|{~Among the new stones there's a coat button, brass, polished by nobody's hands. You put it back where it was.|The new cairn's top stone has a sheaf scratched into it, neat and fresh. You walk on round the hill with your hands in your pockets.}}
opt.right.say.1 [9c757f] = {flag(moor_new_cairn): 你又看了看。自你上次来过之后，有人用红线在它顶上那块石头上系了一枝绿色的什么东西。|{~新石头中间有一颗外套纽扣，黄铜的，亮得不像有谁擦过。你把它放回原处。|新石堆顶上那块石头上刻着一束麦子，又整齐又新。你把手插在兜里，绕着山继续走。}}

@event moor3_warm_turf
# en: The Warm Hill
title [b3c658] = 温暖的山
# en: The turf of the hollow hill is warm, the way a loaf is warm under its cloth, though the fog is cold all round it. When you kneel, you can feel something through your knees, very faint and very regular, like a great slow breath.
text [6fdc78] = 空心山上的草皮是暖的，就像布底下的一条面包那样暖，虽然四周的雾都是冷的。你跪下来时，膝盖能感觉到什么东西，很微弱，很有规律，像一次巨大而缓慢的呼吸。
# en: A student lying with an ear pressed to the turf of a round green hill on a cold, foggy moor, steam rising faintly from the grass around them.
scene [722c6e] = 寒冷的雾蒙蒙的荒原上，一个学生把耳朵贴在一座圆绿山的草皮上躺着，周围的草上隐隐冒着热气。
# en: Get off the hill
opt.left.label [5d9bfc] = 离开这座山
# en: {~You stand up very quickly and walk back down off the hill without looking round.|You leave the warm turf to whatever is warming it, and go home.}
opt.left.say.1 [3e341c] = {~你飞快地站起来，头也不回地走下了山。|你把暖草皮留给不管是什么在暖着它的东西，回家去了。}
# en: Put your ear to the ground
opt.right.label [c53508] = 把耳朵贴到地上
# en: {~Far down, faint as a dream, you hear a fiddle playing, and plates, and a long table being laid. Someone laughs. You get up with grass marks on your cheek and walk on round the hill.|You listen. Under the hill, someone is counting, slowly and happily, and gets to six, and starts again from one.}
opt.right.say.1 [91bb44] = {~在很深的地方，微弱得像一场梦，你听见有人在拉小提琴，有盘子的声音，有一张长桌正在摆开。有人笑了。你站起来时脸颊上印着草痕，绕着山继续走。|你听着。山底下，有人在慢慢地、高高兴兴地数数，数到六，又从一开始。}
# en: Foretell it, out loud
opt.up.label [d766f5] = 大声把它预言出来
# en: {~You say it aloud, into the turf: "Whatever is under this hill will be found out." The warmth goes out of the grass like a held breath let go. You walk on with the words still in your mouth.|You foretell, out loud, that this hill will open. Far below, a fiddle stops in the middle of its tune, and doesn't start again while you're there.}
opt.up.say.1 [8f0158] = {~你对着草皮大声说：“不管这座山底下是什么，都会被人发现。”暖意从草里退了出去，像一口憋着的气终于吐了出来。你继续往前走，话还含在嘴里。|你大声预言，这座山会打开。在很深的地方，一把小提琴在曲子中间停住了，你在的时候，它再没响起。}

@event moor3_bronze
# en: Bronze in the Heather
title [6116b6] = 石楠里的青铜
# en: {flag(moor_bronze_taken): The bronze on the hill's flank is fewer pieces than you left, and not the same ones. The bowl is still there, brimming with rainwater, and beside it someone has laid a new sickle, bright as a coin.|In the heather on the hill's flank, old bronze lies about as if a cart had tipped over a thousand years ago and nobody had bothered to pick it up: a little sickle, a bowl, three rings gone green. All of it is worked with sheaves.}
text [04cb06] = {flag(moor_bronze_taken): 山腰上的青铜比你离开时少了，也不是原来那几件了。那只碗还在，盛满了雨水，旁边有人放了一把新镰刀，亮得像一枚硬币。|在山腰的石楠丛里，旧青铜器散落一地，好像一千年前有辆车在这儿翻了，谁也没费心去捡：一把小镰刀、一只碗、三枚发绿的戒指。每一件上都铸着麦束。}
# en: A scatter of old green bronze objects, a bowl, a sickle, rings, half hidden in heather on the slope of a round hill, a student kneeling over them.
scene [f92ae5] = 一座圆山的山坡上，一堆发绿的旧青铜器半掩在石楠里，一只碗、一把镰刀、几枚戒指，一个学生跪在它们上方。
# en: Leave it and turn back
opt.left.label [d1faaa] = 别管它，回头
# en: {~Some things look as if they were left for someone. You leave them, and go home.|You turn back with empty hands, which feels like the right size of hands to have out here.}
opt.left.say.1 [57ed7e] = {~有些东西看起来是留给某个人的。你没动它们，回家了。|你空着手回去，在这儿，空着手似乎正合适。}
# en: Fill your bag
opt.right.label [37d0f5] = 装满你的包
# en: {~You take the sickle and the rings. The bowl you leave; it feels like someone's. Walking on, the bag is heavier than bronze should be.|You fill your bag. Behind you, a sheep bell rings once, from nowhere you can see.}
opt.right.say.1 [82b760] = {~你拿了镰刀和戒指。碗你留下了；它好像是谁的。往前走时，包比青铜该有的分量还沉。|你装满了包。在你身后，一只羊铃响了一下，从一个你看不见的地方。}

@event moor_hill_door
# en: The Door in the Hill
title [54d853] = 山里的门
# en: {flag(moor_hill_door): The door in the hill again, low and round and shut, its sheaf knocker cold with dew.|Round the far side of the hollow hill, where nobody would see it from the road, there's a door: low and round, old oak gone silver, set into the turf as neatly as a door in a wall. Its knocker is an iron sheaf of wheat. The grass in front of it has been trodden.}
text [e88a13] = {flag(moor_hill_door): 又是山里的那扇门，又矮又圆，关着，麦束门环被露水打得冰凉。|在空心山的另一侧，从路上谁也看不见的地方，有一扇门：又矮又圆，老橡木已经褪成了银色，嵌在草皮里，就像墙上的一扇门那样整齐。门环是一束铁铸的麦子。门前的草被踩过。}
# en: A low round door of weathered oak set into the green turf side of a hill on a foggy moor, an iron knocker shaped like a sheaf of wheat, a student standing before it.
scene [4424dd] = 雾蒙蒙的荒原上，一座山的绿草皮侧面嵌着一扇饱经风霜的低矮圆形橡木门，门环是一束铁铸的麦子，一个学生站在门前。
# en: Leave it shut and go home
opt.left.label [851035] = 让它关着，回家
# en: {~You go back round the hill and down off the moor. Halfway, you realise you've been walking on tiptoe.|You leave the door as you found it. At the third cairn you look back. The fog has hidden the hill.}
opt.left.say.1 [822440] = {~你绕回山的另一边，下了荒原。走到一半，你才发现自己一直踮着脚走。|你让那扇门保持原样。走到第三个石堆时你回头看。雾已经把山藏起来了。}
# en: Knock
opt.right.label [60f31f] = 敲门
# en: {~You lift the sheaf and let it fall. The sound goes down a long way. From very far below, something knocks back, once, and then again, slowly, as if counting, and stops at six. It seems to be waiting for you to give the seventh. You don't.|You knock. Nothing answers, but the turf under your feet goes warm, and stays warm, all the way to the road.}
opt.right.say.1 [6503f6] = {~你提起麦束，让它落下。声音往下传了很远。从很深的地方，有什么东西回敲了一下，又一下，慢慢地，像是在数数，数到六就停了。它好像在等你敲第七下。你没有敲。|你敲了门。没有回应，可你脚下的草皮暖了起来，一直暖到你走回路上。}
